[[string]]
id = "welcome.note"
text = "Picture each charge as a charged balloon in a vacuum, not as an electron. A balloon has a size and bounces off its neighbors. A vacuum means no air drag: the electric force changes the speed, and when the Lorentz force is on the magnetic field turns the path. A soft bounce spends a little energy. An electron has no path to draw, and the Orbit scene is not an atom. The reference (H) says where the model parts from real particles."

[[string]]
id = "welcome.p1"
text = "A sandbox for electric and magnetic fields. Charges sit on the screen and move under the Coulomb and Lorentz forces, and the program draws the field, the potential and the energy. Moving charges make a magnetic field; switch the Lorentz force on (M) to let magnetic fields act on them."

[[string]]
id = "welcome.p2"
text = "Orange is positive, blue is negative. A white ring means pinned: that charge does not move. Dipole, like charges, quadrupole and the capacitor start pinned. Orbit, Rutherford, Swarm, the cyclotron, E×B drift and the coil already have charges in motion. The L key over a charge pins or unpins it."

